;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-14, for Phase 17 (design section 20,
;; proposals 1 to 10, approved by the user); reviewed by the user,
;; 2026-10-14. Why this is right:
;; - cardinal.mod is llvm-cardinal's, built under -O2; on the guest it
;;   prints llvm-cardinal's expected (the Err line on SYS$ERROR).
;; - Widening is zero extension (proposal 1): every CARD8 or CARD16
;;   passed to Show's CARD64 is MOVZBL or MOVZWL then CLRL of the high
;;   longword, a CARD32 MOVL then CLRL; w := a is MOVZBW, d := w MOVZWL,
;;   q := d MOVL and CLRL (line 62, and LONG at 63); 255 + 300 (line 69)
;;   widens a by MOVZBW before ADDW3; the index table[a] (88) and IN's
;;   element (96) are MOVZBL. SYSTEM.VAL(INTEGER, LONG(a)) (76) is
;;   MOVZBW, then CVTWL as an INTEGER for Out.Int; SYSTEM.VAL(CARD32, i)
;;   (77) of an INTEGER extends by i's family, CVTWL, so -1 is 2^32 - 1.
;;   pair.high := pair.low (89) is MOVZBW, so INCW makes 256. SHORT(w)
;;   (64), without -range-checks, is CVTWB, the low byte (300 is 44).
;; - Arithmetic stays at the CARD's width and wraps: ADDB3 (47, 300 is
;;   44), DECB (48, 255), INCW (49, 0), ADDL3 #1 (50, 0), ADDL2/ADWC
;;   (51, 0), MULB2 (52, 0), MNEGB (53, 253), Bump's ADDW2 #-25536, the
;;   word whose bits are 40000 (line 42; 30000 + 40000 is 4464).
;; - Comparisons are unsigned (proposal 2): BLEQU, BLSSU and BGEQU after
;;   CMPB (line 56); a CARD64's (57) compares the high longwords with
;;   BGTRU/BLSSU, then the low ones with BLEQU; = and # stay BNEQ/BEQL.
;; - DIV and MOD (proposal 3): a CARD8's (58) is MOVZBL, DIVL3 #7, and
;;   the remainder by MULL3/SUBL3, the result MOVZBL'd for Show; a
;;   CARD64's (59) calls POC_CDIV and POC_CMOD with the addresses of q
;;   and of the divisor's quadword; Halve's CARD32 (37) is MOVL/CLRL R1
;;   then POC_HDIV, taking R0.
;; - To a real (proposal 4): a CARD8 is MOVZBL then CVTLG (65); a CARD64
;;   calls POC_CTOG with q's address (66), its G_floating in R0/R1;
;;   a * 1.5 (67) is a REAL: MOVZBL, CVTLF, MULF2, then CVTFG.
;; - Shifts (proposal 5): ASH(a, -1) of a CARD8 (84) is MOVZBL, ASHL #-1
;;   and BICL2 #^X80000000, the logical shift, then MOVZBL; ASH(a, 1) is
;;   ASHL #1, MOVZBL keeping its own type's 8 bits (0); ASH(q, -63) (85)
;;   is ASHQ #-1, BICL2 #^X80000000 of R1, then ASHQ #-62. LSH (86) is the
;;   same as ASH of a CARD; ROT is unchanged (MULL2 #257, ASHL, ASHL #-8).
;; - The checked and identity ones (proposal 6): ABS(a) (95) is a itself
;;   (MOVZBL for Show); CHR(a) of a CARD8 is MOVB, no test; ODD is BICB3
;;   #254. table[a] checks a against 255 unsigned (CMPL #255, BLEQU)
;;   and traps 2 above it (PUSHL #2).
;; - Constants (proposal 7): a CARD32's or CARD64's above the signed
;;   range is hexadecimal (#^XFFFFFFFF, #^XFFFFFFFD, #^X80000000);
;;   bytes and words stay decimal, #200, #250, #255, #65535 (MOVB, CMPB,
;;   MOVW), which MACRO assembles to the same bits.
;; - CASE a OF (92) is a CASEB table of 256 entries, 0..127 low, 128..254
;;   high, 255 max: CASEB's selector less #0 is compared unsigned with
;;   the limit, so a CARD8 above 127 indexes its own entry.
;; - FOR (proposal 8): counting down to 0 (99), the head's TSTB with
;;   BGEQU (always true unsigned) and the end SUBB3 #0, a, against #1,
;;   so it ends at 0 (6 times, a = 0); up to 255 (100), CMPB #255 BLEQU
;;   and SUBB3 a, #255, ending at 255; BY 100 (101) ends at 200; the
;;   CARD64 loop up to MAX (102) takes its distance as a quadword, SUBL2
;;   and SBWC from #^XFFFFFFFF twice, compared unsigned with 1. The
;;   INTEGER FOR of line 90 is signed as before, with the new end.
;; - The text procedures (proposal 9): Out.Card and CardHex, Err.Card
;;   and CardHex, OutStr.Card and CardHex and InStr.Card are called with
;;   G^ and their HUGEINT arguments as addresses of quadword copies;
;;   InStr.Done is read as a global byte (BLBS G^INSTR_DONE_...).
;;   Each module's key is the one its own expected file shows.
; cardinal, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
	.TITLE	CARDINAL
	.IDENT	/ef731fb7b7900f58/
